## Conversation Summary

Date: 2026-09-25

### Objective

Implement the librarian orchestration and controller boundaries that expose librarian features without moving business rules into the UI or CLI.

### Key decisions

- Keep `LibrarianController` thin and delegate rules to services.
- Check librarian authorization before invoking collaborators.
- Use integration contracts for member, catalogue, book-copy, and loan operations.
- Forward service failures to the view boundary instead of exposing repository details.

### Work completed

- Added controller coverage for member registration/edit/deactivation/search, book operations, damaged/lost copies, loan queries, reservations, fines, and alert delivery.
- Verified injected-clock behaviour for overdue queries and validation of reservation reminders.
- Added CLI workflow coverage for login/logout, protected commands, malformed arguments, searches, reservations, fines, notifications, and persistence across sessions.

